## What the tests check

| File | Case | Checks |
|---|---|---|
| `outline_test` | Each room gets its own outline, and the wall between them is in both | 2 rooms with a door, 4 sides each; both faces of the shared wall near x = 1.75 |
| `outline_steps_test` | An L-shaped room has two walls facing the same way | A5 |
| | A door does not split the wall it is in | A5 |
| | A short thing against the wall is covered | A5 |
| | A thing longer than `dent_length` stays a wall | A5 |
| | Two walls that stop short are stretched to meet | A6 |
| | A wall that pokes past is trimmed back | A6 |
| | A perpendicular wall that runs on far is not a corner | A6 |
| `walls_test` | Faces from two rooms make one wall as thick as their distance | B1 |
| | A face from one room makes a wall of default thickness | B1 |

B2 to B5 have no test of their own.

## Gaps found

| What | Where |
|---|---|
| **Thickness is measured only for a wall shared by two rooms** (faces 5 to 35 cm apart). In a one-room map every wall gets the default 10 cm. The twin does not say which thickness is measured and which is assumed | `walls.cpp` |
| **Right angles only.** A side is on the x or the y axis of the squared map | `outline.cpp` |
| If the wall was not seen, the walk ends on the furniture in front of it, and the furniture becomes the "wall". Only the dent rules (short and shallow) undo this | `outline.cpp` |
| Furniture longer than `dent_length` = 2.0 m within 50 cm of the wall counts as a wall | `outline.cpp` |
| A wall farther than `max_reach` = 1.5 m from the free floor is not found | `outline.cpp` |
| The wall step uses **two bands**: `outline.band_lo` = 10 cm for the walk, `candidates.band_lo` = 30 cm for counting dots and picking out furniture | `model.cpp`, `walls.cpp` |
| The pairing limits 5 and 35 cm are fixed numbers, not settings | `walls.cpp` |
| B2 to B5 have no test | `backend/tests/` |
